; GoldBot -- FTMO 2-Step Phase 1, prop-firm mode preset.
; Base strategy: daily2-ai-s5-slwide-smcnorm (PF ~3.2, win ~65%, verified report
;   mt5/backtests/reports/GoldBot-real-daily2-ai-s5-slwide-smcnorm-ai-s5-2y.htm).
; Firm contract reused verbatim from the proven mt5/Presets/PropGuard/ftmo-2step-p1.set:
; 5% daily loss, 10% STATIC max DD, Phase 1 target 10%. See
; mt5/backtests/PROPGUARD_DESIGN.md for the frozen rule list this implements.
;
; InpPropChallengeRiskPct=0.50 is derived, not copied from PropGuard's 1.00: GoldBot's
; ladder places up to 3 legs per signal, and journal sampling of daily2-ai-s5-slwide-
; smcnorm's unscaled 2y report (mt5/backtests/reports/...-ai-s5-2y.trades.csv, early
; 'Pending order placed' lines, e.g. lot=0.04 entry=2334.89 sl=2332.00 -> riskCash
; ~=lot*|entry-sl|*100 ~=1.16% of the $1000 starting equity for that single leg, ~1.7%
; combined across a 2-leg signal) put GoldBot's own unscaled per-signal risk-taking in
; the ~1.5-3% of equity range -- consistent with mt5/backtests/PROPGUARD_GOLDBOT_SIM.md's
; k=1 finding that unscaled GoldBot risk breaches the 10% static max-DD floor too often
; over 1y/2y. Targeting PROPGUARD_GOLDBOT_SIM.md's winning k=1/3 operating point against
; that ~1.5% baseline lands at ~0.50% base risk per signal -- NOT a precise backsolve
; (small sample, assumes standard 100oz/$0.01-tick XAUUSD contract, ignores the high-
; conviction 1.5x score bump and per-path lotMultiplier layered on top downstream, see
; mt5/Include/GoldBot/PropMode.mqh's GoldBotPropCostAndSizingGate header comment) --
; flagged for recalibration against a real prop-mode-ON backtest before committing a
; challenge fee, per PROPGUARD_GOLDBOT_SIM.md §8 caveat 1.
;
